    text: "Procedure extract: Head-lice return rule\n\nBanksia Park School sets the following rule.\n\nFrom the day the note goes home, a student with live lice may return after the first treatment recommended on the health sheet. A student sent back for the whole week with no treatment advice should go to home only until the first recommended treatment is done. A student who has been treated that morning may still go in class the same day. The note does not name individual students. A separate date, the next staff meeting, applies only if a teacher asks for spare copies.\n\nThe stated reason is that the health sheet says one treatment is enough for return, with a second treatment later. It does not claim that the school can diagnose lice by email.",
