    text: "Subject: Library overdue pause\n\nHello colleagues,\n\nFrom Monday 8 September, a student with an item more than three weeks overdue may not borrow a new item until it is returned or paid for. A new borrow by a student with a four-week overdue novel should go to the returns desk first. A student whose books are one week overdue may still go in a new borrow. In-library reading during class time is still allowed. A separate date, Friday 12 September, applies only if a family asks for a reprint of the loan list.\n\nThe stated reason is that long overdues were leaving popular titles off the shelf. It does not claim that a small fine deletes the student's library membership forever.\n\nThanks,\nYarra Bend Primary",
