    text: "Procedure extract: Assessment extension requests\n\nMallee East School sets the following rule.\n\nFrom the start of next term, an extension must be requested before the due time, unless the absence is unexpected on the day. A request made two days after a known due time with no unexpected absence should go to the faculty, but it does not meet this rule. A request made the day before a known due time may still go in the faculty leader. The rule does not mark the task for the student. A separate date, the week before the holidays, applies only if a family asks how the form looks.\n\nThe stated reason is that late requests after a known deadline were hard to judge fairly. It does not claim that every extension is automatic if a parent sends any email.",
